// The residual spread of the closes about the least squares line fitted through
// them, which is what makes it an error rather than a deviation.
//
// Exercises: three loops over the same window inside one bar, the history
// operator read at a distance the loop decides rather than the source, and a
// divisor of two less than the length because two degrees of freedom went into
// the fitted line.

version 1

study("Standard error", precision = 6)

len = input(14, "Length", min = 3, max = 2000)

// The ladder of positions is the same on every bar, and it is written out
// rather than reduced to a closed form so that the sum has the order the study
// was defined with.
centre = (len + 1) / 2

total = 0.0
for k = 0 to len - 1
    total = total + close[k]
middle = total / len

spread = 0.0
tilt  = 0.0
ladder = 0.0
for k = 0 to len - 1
    fromMean = middle - close[k]
    pos = centre - k - 1
    spread = spread + fromMean * fromMean
    tilt  = tilt + pos * fromMean
    ladder = ladder + pos * pos

plot(sqrt((spread - (tilt * tilt) / ladder) / (len - 2)), "Standard error", orange, width = 2)
